Ladybird still visits every node of the accessibility tree on each
build, but it decides which nodes to send from version numbers and
the few fields every build computes again, rather than comparing each
node’s data with the last tree sent. The other engines keep track of
dirty objects and visit only those. Blink’s AXObjectCacheImpl marks
objects dirty, and AXTreeSerializer::SerializeChanges() serializes
just those. WebKit’s AXObjectCache queues updates for single nodes
of its AXIsolatedTree, through AXIsolatedTree::queueNodeUpdate(). And
Gecko’s DocAccessible::QueueCacheUpdate() records which cache domains of
which accessibles to send.
